  "question": "The vector $\\vec{r}$ divides the line segment from $\\vec{a} = 2\\hat{i} - 4\\hat{j} + 3\\hat{k}$ to $\\vec{b} = 5\\hat{i} + 2\\hat{j} - \\hat{k}$ in the ratio $k:1$ externally. If $\\vec{r}$ is perpendicular to $\\vec{a}$, find the value(s) of $k$.",
  "answeroption": "A",
  "explanation": "Section formula (external division):<br /><br />$\\vec{r} = \\dfrac{k \\vec{b} -\\vec{a}}{k-1}$<br /><br />Set $\\vec{r} \\cdot \\vec{a} = 0$:<br /><br />$\\left( \\dfrac{k \\vec{b} - \\vec{a}}{k-1} \\right) \\cdot \\vec{a} = 0$<br /><br />$k \\vec{b} \\cdot \\vec{a} - \\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{a} = 0$<br /><br />$k (\\vec{b} \\cdot \\vec{a}) = \\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{a}$<br /><br />$k = \\dfrac{\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{a}}{\\vec{b} \\cdot \\vec{a}}$<br /><br />Compute:<br /><br />$\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{a} = 2^2 + (-4)^2 + 3^2 = 4 + 16 + 9 = 29$<br /><br />$\\vec{b} \\cdot \\vec{a} = (5)(2) + (2)(-4) + (-1)(3) = 10 - 8 - 3 = -1$<br /><br />So $k = 29/(-1) = -29$<br /><br />Therefore, $k = -29$.",
